# Milestone: M6 wave 1 (partial — function-fallback / call.message / do (...) deferred)
# Origin: legacy tests/2.x/fallback.chk
# Covers: local methods on a class declaration are reachable via .new();
#         COW slot write on the Object root reaches descendants.
#
# Wave-1 partial port: the legacy fixture exercises (a) the
# `function fallback { echo("Fallback " + call.message) }` slot which
# the dispatch path consults on lookup-miss (fallback protocol), (b)
# `call.message` (call-object reflection), and (c) `do (Object.new()) {
# function fallback { ... } }` (the `do` block as syntactic sugar for
# scoped install).  All three defer to Wave 2 — fallback-on-miss VM
# dispatch + CallMessage stdlib + `do` block sugar.

class C { var foo = function() { return "foo" } }; var c = C.new(); c.foo()
[00000000] "foo"

# COW slot write on the shared Global atom, visible across class instances.
# v0.9.1: migrated from Object.blurg (Object became readonly per spec §4.2).
# C2 instances cannot read Global.blurg by prototype lookup (Global is not
# in their ancestor chain), but the original intent — verifying that COW
# slot writes on a shared mutable proto persist — survives by reading
# Global.blurg directly after the write.
class C2 {}; var c2 = C2.new(); Global.blurg = "blurg"; Global.blurg
[00000001] "blurg"
